# Labels for the namespaces Kates creates or deploys into.
#
# Copy this file to .labels (git-ignored) in the directory you run kates in,
# and uncomment or add lines. kates deploy, kates auto, kates detect, kates
# kyverno apply and the kates migrate commands that create lab namespaces read
# ./.labels, or the file --labels-file names; scripts/common.sh's
# ensure_namespace reads ./.labels.
#
# Format: one key=value per line. Spaces around the key and the value are
# trimmed; blank lines and lines whose first non-space character is # are
# skipped. There are no inline comments and no quotes: a # or a quote inside
# a value is invalid. A repeated key is an error.
#
# Precedence, per key, later wins: .labels, then KATES_NAMESPACE_LABELS
# (comma-separated key=value), then each --namespace-label flag.
#
# Keys: an optional DNS-subdomain prefix and a /, then a name of 1-63
# characters [A-Za-z0-9-_.] that starts and ends alphanumeric. Values: empty,
# or 1-63 characters under the same rule.
# Reserved prefixes are refused: kubernetes.io, k8s.io, helm.sh, strimzi.io,
# kates.io and their subdomains (app.kubernetes.io/... too), except
# pod-security.kubernetes.io exactly.

# team=payments
# segment=payments
# cost-center=4711
# pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce=restricted
